DESCRIPTION: FIND: `bench/dm/_manager.py`, `_get_current_metric()` and `bench/dm/_immune.py`, `_verify_remediation_outcomes()` have no support for per-model metrics, yet multiple chains target per-model pathologies (`parser_yield`, `monotonic_decline`, `cpf_spike`, `verification_miscalibration`) and still verify against global `finding_count`. This exact global/per-model mismatch has been noted in prior findings, but the missed concrete defect is that the verification interface itself cannot express scoped metrics at all. Evidence: `_get_current_metric(metric_name: str)` accepts only a bare name and returns only global histories; `_verify_remediation_outcomes()` reads `state["target_metric"]` and pulls only global histories as well. Therefore even if chain-state scoping is fixed, the verification machinery still cannot verify the intended per-model recovery signal. A parser directive for model X is declared successful if total system findings rise, even if model X remains unparsable.
