DESCRIPTION: FIND: `bench/dm/_manager.py`, `apply_diagnosis()` can queue a `DEFER` remediation even when the underlying transform is already impossible or a no-op, because the DEFER decision is made before any feasibility check. Evidence: for a DEFER step, the function immediately appends to `_deferred_remediations` and returns `None`, without checking whether the target is already at floor/bound or already applied. Concrete examples in shown code: `lower_tau_sim_to_floor` is pointless when `tau_sim == 0.3`; `halve_tau_vocab` step 1 becomes pointless when `tau_vocab_growth == 0.01`; `lower_feasibility_threshold` is pointless at floor `0.70`; `flag_verification_unreliable` is pointless if model is already in `_verification_unreliable_models`. This produces approval queue spam and human-review work for actions that cannot change system state.
PROPOSED_FIX: FIX: preflight the transform before queueing DEFER by adding a non-mutating applicability check.

